    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. The audit line confirms the new behavior: `membershipLevel=3` (1 base + email + namesakeCount 0, capped at 3).\n\nSummary of the change \u2014 I replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string property with `membershipLevel`, an `int32` (min 1, max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced `membershipTier(Owner)` with `public int membershipLevel(Owner)`: start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3. Updated the `@Mapping` target accordingly and removed the now-unused `householdSize` helper (the old GOLD/household logic is gone).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (via `ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner)`) instead of relating to the old tier.\n\nTests: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. The new acceptance test (`membershipLevel` = 3 for an owner with an email and a unique name) passes, and the field maps correctly through the generated DTO on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.",
